<title>USA: RESEARCH ALERT - Kellogg cut to sell.</title>
<headline>RESEARCH ALERT - Kellogg cut to sell.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-06-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>SBC Warburg analyst Chris Jakubik said Friday he cut his rating on cereal giant Kellogg Co to sell from reduce based on valuation.</p>
<p>-- &quot;Recent outperformance (of Kellogg's stock) has made valuation vulnerable...,&quot; Jakubik said.</p>
<p>-- The analyst, however, raised earnings estimates for Kellogg to $3.25 from $3.20 for 1997 and to $3.55 from $3.50 for 1998. He cited lower interest expense and recent market share gains in the domestic cereal market.</p>
<p>-- Kellogg shares were up 3/16 to 82-15/16.</p>
<p>((Reuters Chicago Newsdesk (312) 408-8787))</p>
